# local tooling — Claude Code settings + worktrees, never product code
.claude/
# ...except the SHARED project settings. A cloud runner has no way to be granted a
# permission interactively, so the one rule it cannot start without - the read-only
# rclone verbs that fetch the corpus - has to travel with the repo. Personal and
# machine-local settings stay ignored.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.DS_Store
_archive/Kinley/ra-port-2026-07-16/

# browser-session console logs from local tooling — never a deliverable
.playwright-mcp/

.superpowers/

# decrypted corpus copies and generated packages — derived from Drive,
# hold real contract numbers and rents, never committed
_archive/corpus-cache/

# rendered screenshots from `node app/full-mp/shots.js` — derived from the
# build on every run, and binaries never belong in this repo
app/full-mp/_shots/

# The sweep's RECORDS are the deliverable and must be committed; its generated
# DOCUMENTS are not. sweep.js writes both under --out: one JSON per package at the
# top, and every PDF and workbook it produced under _out/. Pointing --out at a
# tracked path (necessary, because the default sits beyond a symlink and git will
# not track it at all) would otherwise commit hundreds of megabytes of output that
# is regenerated by the next run anyway.
docs/superpowers/plans/sweep-out/_out/
